# ---------------- ItemData.events (Task 9 E7: item bases) ----------------
# Item bases for the affix generator. `spawn Ring at me rarity "Rare" level 12` looks the base up
# here, rolls the rarity's affixes from AffixData.events and writes the result onto the spawned
# clone as its own `my` variables (my damage, my FireResist, my Rarity, my ItemName, my ItemLevel).
#
# HOW IT LOADS: read by name — ItemData.events — when events load and on hot reload, before any
# actor's `me appears`, exactly like WeaponData.events and EnemyTypes.events.
#
# FIELDS (per base, one variable each — the base name plus the field):
#   <Base>Slot        the equip slot this base wants (`my RingSlot`, E5 is content only)
#   <Base>Damage      base damage the item grants (applied on `equip`)
#   <Base>Armor       base armor the item grants (applied on `equip`)
#   <Base>ItemLevel   the item level this base is meant for (informational)
#
# A base that exists only as `<Base><Field>` globals is a valid base. Item names must be ONE
# word: the bag and `equip` take single tokens (`Ring`, not `Rare Ring`).

when game starts
  set RingSlot to "ring"
  set RingDamage to 0
  set RingArmor to 0
  set RingItemLevel to 1

  set AmuletSlot to "amulet"
  set AmuletDamage to 0
  set AmuletArmor to 0
  set AmuletItemLevel to 1

  set SwordSlot to "weapon"
  set SwordDamage to 12
  set SwordArmor to 0
  set SwordItemLevel to 1
